  "worked_solution": "The graph consists of $2$ parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-1,3]$ and the arc of a semi-circle for $x\\in [3,5].$ Therefore, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{\u23df}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{\u23df}}_{{A}_{2}}\n$$\n\nThe $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-1,3].$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+4)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [3,5].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =5+\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
